
prt‐cache(8)			      System Manager’s Manual			       prt‐cache(8)

NAME
     prt-cache - call prt-get using a cache file as a data source

SYNOPSIS
     prt-cache command [options] <arguments>

DESCRIPTION
     prt-cache	is  a  synonym	for  prt-get  ‐‐cache.	 It’s perfectly the same as calling prt-get
     ‐‐cache, just shorter. See man prt‐get(8) for details on how to use prt‐get

     Even though there are almost restrictions on using prt‐cache over prt‐get, it’s mostly  recom‐
     mended  for  the  following  commands:  search,  dsearch, list, info, depends, quickdep, diff,
     quickdiff and info.  It won’t work for the dup command.

     Using prt‐cache isinst is not recommended (really not!)

     Note that if the cache is not up to date (and there’s a newer port in the	ports  tree),  prt‐
     cache install and prt‐cache update will use the version from the ports tree anyway, so there’s
     no real risk.

     If	 you’re	 using	prt‐cache,  make sure to regenerate the cache by calling prt‐get cache each
     time you make changes to the ports tree!

     To create a cache, just invoke prt‐get cache.  Make sure you have the right permissions to	 do
     this

